<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peltuinum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peltuinum was an ancient town of the Vestini on a high plateau near Prata d'Ansidonia in the province of L'Aquila, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abruzzo">Abruzzo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. It grew as a stopping place on the drove road used by flocks moving between the mountains and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, and became a Roman municipium on the Via Claudia Nova. Its ruins include walls, a temple and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peltuinum.jpg" alt="Peltuinum" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Stemonitis · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peltuinum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
